  "research": "Same flat-bench body as neutral_grip_dumbbell_press (root rot -98, z 0.55 estimate; probe_bench to tune). Dumbbell ~0.36 m long (half 0.18). Start elev 88 / plane 93: hand x = 0.22 - 0.6 sin3 = 0.19 -> inner ends ~0.01 from the midline each (gap ~2 cm, 'almost touching'); pronated axis [-1,0,0]. End elev 82 / plane 45: du = (0.70, 0.70, 0.14), E = (0.40, 0.20, -0.04); fold toward the midline and chest (bend [-1,-0.2,-0.2]) gives bperp (-0.70, 0.70, -0.14); elbow 115: forearm = (-0.93, 0.34, -0.19), hand = E + 0.33 fore = (0.10, 0.32, -0.10) torso. Handle tipped so its inner end points at the chest: the -X axis turned 70 deg with the forearm = (-0.34, -0.94, -0.07); inner plate reaches ~0.15 above the shoulder line = chest surface (~0.12). Hands at x +-0.10 put the two inner plates (r 0.088) about touching at the midline; if they overlap, lower elbow to 110. pole [1,0,0] keeps the elbows pointing out. S1 Muscle & Strength Tate press profile, S2 Boehler 2011. QA 11 Nov: body arched off the end of the flat pad (rot -98 + 27 deg spine arch); now lies flat (rot -90, spine -1 each)."
